    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1986, by its Section 3401(a)(1), requires the Commission to assess and collect fees and annual charges in any fiscal year in amounts equal to all of the costs incurred by the Commission in a fiscal year. For the purposes of recovering this payment, this Section establishes a FERC ACA Unit Charge to be applicable to all jurisdictional transportation quantities transported. These costs will continue to be recovered under its current rates with customers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Authorization of the cash out program was granted in Docket #RP07-7174, issued July 31, 2008, 24 FERC &#182; 61,121. Based on activity, the result can either be a regulatory asset or liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC 740 considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Respondent is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283. This accounting is also outlined in FERC Docket AI93-5-000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In Docket No. RP18-250-000 effective January 15, 2018 Columbia Gulf filed to change the accounting for the Transportation Retainage Adjustment to either be a regulatory asset or liability from account 186.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the difference between the expense recognized in rates and accrual basis accounting. Recognition of expense is in accordance with FERC Docket No. RP11-1435. Accrual basis accounting is in accordance with ASC 715.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This balance represents the impact of U.S. Tax Reform as applied to businesses subject to rate-regulated accounting. The regulatory liability will be amortized over varying terms that approximate the expected reversal of the underlying deferred tax assets and liabilities that gave rise to the regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In Docket No. RP18-250-000 effective January 15, 2018 Columbia Gulf filed to change the accounting for the Transportation Retainage Adjustment to either be a regulatory asset or liability from account 186.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Uses include, but are not limited to, flow tests, blowing drips, running pigs/spheres, blowing down lines,well construction, compressor station blowdowns, and starts and stops.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The volumes used to calculate the Annual Charge Assessment are 1,254,727,195 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Retainage volumes reported by Respondent are actual volumes retained by contract type (Discounted, Negotiated, orRecourse.)</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent uses a monthly average spot rate as the basis for valuing gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Respondent does not track Gas Used or Lost and Unaccounted For by contract type.&#160; For reporting purposes, Gas Used and Lost and Unaccounted For are allocated between contract types (discounted, negotiated, and recourse) on the basis of all actual receipt volumes recorded on TRA rate schedules.&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accounts debited include 824, 856,858,859.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Respondent has a Commission approved Transportation Retainage Adjustment (TRA) that tracks shipper supplied gas. Any excess or deficient balance is included in the next annual filing and collected or passed back, as appropriate, through a positive or negative surcharge to the newly established rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Expenses (including taxes) includes estimated property taxes. These facilities are not separately reported to taxing agencies nor separately assessed by taxing agencies.&#160; In addition, tax bills for distinct facilities are not received in the states in which these facilities reside.&#160; Cost and accumulated depreciation data has been used by the respondent to develop reasonable estimates of the property taxes incurred on these facilities.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The incremental project utilizes the prevailing system fuel rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">East Lateral XPress Project burned 1,400,768 Dths and retained 1,249,918&#160; Dths in 2025.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Income taxes are recorded in accordance with the Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed contributions/distributions recorded in Other Paid in Capital.&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; The volumes used to calculate the Annual Charge Adjustment are 1,254,727,195 Dth.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">See Notes to Financial Statements - Transactions with Affiliated Companies for the basis of allocated expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The compressors are owned and operated by third party.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">New unit in service April 25, 2025; Unit 1 is 23,502 HP</link:footnote>
